# Environment for the control server. Copy to snipe.env (gitignored) and fill in.
#
#   cp snipe.env.example snipe.env
#   nano snipe.env
#   chmod 600 snipe.env
#
# Then start the server with:
#   set -a && source snipe.env && set +a && npm run snipe:server

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The only thing standing between the internet and your wallets. Generate one:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
SNIPE_TOKEN=

# ── Telegram summaries (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Token from @BotFather (/newbot). Chat id: message your bot once, then open
#   https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates
# and read result[0].message.chat.id
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ── Optional tuning ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SNIPE_PORT=8787
# SNIPE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Restrict which site may drive this server (default "*" is fine behind a
# tunnel + token, but narrowing costs nothing):
# SNIPE_ORIGINS=https://launchpad-44c.pages.dev
# How far ahead of a stage a job is armed, in ms:
# SNIPE_ARM_LEAD_MS=120000

# The endpoints this box reads and mints through, best first. Comma or
# newline separated. Without it every read goes to the chain's public RPC,
# which meters — a scan then spends its time being rate-limited and split
# into ever smaller pieces. The panel can also push an endpoint down, but
# that depends on which browser last visited; this does not.
# SNIPE_RPCS=https://robinhood-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/YOUR_MINT_KEY
#
# Optional second key, for the scanner, the live feed, the calendar and the
# profit report. A provider's throughput limit is per key, so on one key a
# calendar refresh can be spending the allowance at the second a stage opens,
# and the request that loses is the one that cannot be retried. Set this and
# the heavy reads can never stand in a mint's way. Unset, they share the key
# above, which is fine until the scanning gets busy.
# SNIPE_SCAN_RPCS=https://robinhood-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/YOUR_SCAN_KEY
